    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>CONFRONT \u2013 Face Your Fears</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An abandoned building. Nothing but silence... and something watching you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Confront is a first-person psychological survival horror game that pulls you into a haunting nightmare. In this forsaken place dominated by loneliness and paranoia, the line between reality and illusion begins to blur as your sanity slowly fades.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tense atmosphere and immersive environmental storytelling</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sanity system with hallucinations that intensify over time</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive environments and cryptic clues</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your choices may keep you alive... or not</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>True horror comes from within.</strong><br>If you're ready, don\u2019t close your eyes \u2014 you may never know what\u2019s real again.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>CONFRONT \u2013 Face Your Fears</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An abandoned building. Nothing but silence... and something watching you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Confront is a first-person psychological survival horror game that pulls you into a haunting nightmare. In this forsaken place dominated by loneliness and paranoia, the line between reality and illusion begins to blur as your sanity slowly fades.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tense atmosphere and immersive environmental storytelling</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sanity system with hallucinations that intensify over time</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive environments and cryptic clues</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your choices may keep you alive... or not</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>True horror comes from within.</strong><br>If you're ready, don\u2019t close your eyes \u2014 you may never know what\u2019s real again.</p>",
